				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-26T15:46:52.572Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://yatil.social/@yatil\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>yatil</span></a></span> clearly a 🏆.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.11ty.dev/speedlify/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">11ty.dev/speedlify/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a> is 8104! we’re all in this one together</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114229765331221934",
			"parentId": "114229280445124572",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@polarbirke/114229765306831367",
			"author": {
				"name": "Søren Birkemeyer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@polarbirke",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/802/839/296/356/original/5c89c42a0ceea90b.gif"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-26T16:51:33.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alesroubicek\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>alesroubicek</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> You're right!</p><p>But… it depends on the scenario.</p><p>Sure, if you scroll down into the future until you load events for Christmas, you'll get to 16k. </p><p>There's filter by month feature though and the server returns a new page with (again) only events for the first 7 days of that month.</p><p>Also, most visitors either look for events that happen soon (like, within a fortnight, because they're local) or far away (like, in a few months because they're tourists arriving on vacation).</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114229789357915988",
			"parentId": "114229765331221934",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@polarbirke/114229789339002025",
			"author": {
				"name": "Søren Birkemeyer",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@polarbirke",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/802/839/296/356/original/5c89c42a0ceea90b.gif"
			},
			"date": "2025-03-26T16:57:40.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@alesroubicek\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>alesroubicek</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Not sure if a native virtual scroller would be needed or if content-visibility is going to be the catch-all already, but obviously we and the state opera are nowhere near the end of the journey.</p><p>I just wanted to make a (small) case that the DOM node threshold can lead to something good. 😁</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
